{{!
    @template enrol_apply/decision_controls

    The three things a decider may say about an application: which groups the applicant
    joins, which role they are given, and what to tell them.

    Rendered by both decision surfaces - the queue, which decides several applications at
    once, and the single-application review page - so that the two cannot drift. Neither
    page renders the other, so the fixed element ids below never appear twice on a page.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * hasgroups boolean - whether the course has any group to offer
    * grouplabel string - label of the group chooser
    * grouphelp string - hint explaining what choosing nothing does
    * groups array - list of id and name pairs, one per group in the course; each name is the
      plain spelling, because the option text is output through a double stash and Mustache
      escapes it there
    * hasroles boolean - whether the decider may assign any role in this course
    * rolelabel string - label of the role chooser
    * rolehelp string - hint explaining what choosing nothing does
    * roledefault string - text of the option that leaves the method's own role in charge
    * roles array - list of id and name pairs, one per role the decider may assign; each name is
      the ESCAPED spelling and is therefore output through a TRIPLE stash, exactly as core's own
      element-select.mustache does. The renderer normalises the list through format_string()
      first, because get_assignable_roles() returns a MIXED one - a role carrying a name of its
      own comes back escaped, while the roles a stock site ships come back as bare language
      strings that have never been escaped at all.
    * messagelabel string - label of the optional message to the applicant
    * messagehelp string - hint explaining who reads the message and when
    * messagevalue string - what the operator had already typed, non-empty only on the way back
      from the cancel confirmation; plain spelling, escaped by the double stash
    * notelabel string - label of the decider's own note
    * notehelp string - hint saying who reads the note and who does not
    * notevalue string - the note the operator had already typed, non-empty only on the way back
      from the cancel confirmation. It is NOT pre-filled with the note already stored on the
      application: the writer clears on empty on purpose, so a pre-filled box would carry one
      decision's reason silently into the next. The stored note is shown in the panel above

    Example context (json):
    {
        "hasgroups": true,
        "grouplabel": "Groups to join on approval",
        "grouphelp": "Leave empty to use the groups configured on the enrolment method.",
        "groups": [
            {"id": 3, "name": "Tutorial A"},
            {"id": 4, "name": "R&D < Team"}
        ],
        "hasroles": true,
        "rolelabel": "Role to assign on approval",
        "rolehelp": "Leave it alone to use the role configured on the enrolment method.",
        "roledefault": "Use the enrolment method's role",
        "roles": [
            {"id": 5, "name": "Student"},
            {"id": 3, "name": "R&amp;D &lt; Team"}
        ],
        "messagelabel": "Message to the applicant",
        "messagehelp": "Included in the message they receive. Optional.",
        "messagevalue": "",
        "notelabel": "Note for the record",
        "notehelp": "Kept with the application for whoever looks at it next. The applicant never sees it.",
        "notevalue": ""
    }
}}
{{#hasgroups}}
    <div class="enrol_apply-decisiongroups mt-3">
        <label class="form-label" for="enrol_apply_groups">{{grouplabel}}</label>
        <select class="form-select" id="enrol_apply_groups" name="groups[]" multiple
            aria-describedby="enrol_apply_groups_help">
            {{#groups}}
                <option value="{{id}}">{{name}}</option>
            {{/groups}}
        </select>
        <div class="form-text" id="enrol_apply_groups_help">{{grouphelp}}</div>
    </div>
{{/hasgroups}}
{{#hasroles}}
    <div class="enrol_apply-decisionrole mt-3">
        <label class="form-label" for="enrol_apply_roleid">{{rolelabel}}</label>
        <select class="form-select" id="enrol_apply_roleid" name="roleid"
            aria-describedby="enrol_apply_roleid_help">
            <option value="0">{{roledefault}}</option>
            {{#roles}}
                <option value="{{id}}">{{{name}}}</option>
            {{/roles}}
        </select>
        <div class="form-text" id="enrol_apply_roleid_help">{{rolehelp}}</div>
    </div>
{{/hasroles}}
<div class="enrol_apply-outcomemessage mt-3">
    <label class="form-label" for="enrol_apply_outcomemessage">{{messagelabel}}</label>
    <textarea class="form-control" id="enrol_apply_outcomemessage" name="outcomemessage"
        rows="3" aria-describedby="enrol_apply_outcomemessage_help">{{messagevalue}}</textarea>
    <div class="form-text" id="enrol_apply_outcomemessage_help">{{messagehelp}}</div>
</div>
<div class="enrol_apply-decisionnote mt-3">
    <label class="form-label" for="enrol_apply_decisionnote">{{notelabel}}</label>
    <textarea class="form-control" id="enrol_apply_decisionnote" name="decisionnote"
        rows="3" aria-describedby="enrol_apply_decisionnote_help">{{notevalue}}</textarea>
    <div class="form-text" id="enrol_apply_decisionnote_help">{{notehelp}}</div>
</div>
